&lt;p&gt;Non-ergodic refers to the difference that exists between an individual doing one thing many times, and a group of people doing the same thing once. In this sense, the series of posts featured in this blog will explore concepts that may or may not be mainstream in a &amp;ldquo;survivalistic&amp;rdquo; manner–looking at permanence over time dependent solutions.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
